---
/**
 * Downloads, and the verification the installer already does.
 *
 * The artifacts come from src/lib/release.ts, which derives them from the
 * changelog: this page never spells a version or a file name. The passages
 * about verification are lifted by scripts/download.mjs out of install.sh and
 * the release workflow, with their line ranges.
 *
 * WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. A digest and a byte size are facts about a
 * published artifact, which is on the network, and the build has no network.
 * So this page tells a reader where the digests are rather than printing
 * numbers it cannot have read.
 */
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import Measure from "../components/Measure.astro";
import Lifted from "../components/Lifted.astro";
import download from "../generated/download.json";
import { latestRelease, releases, releaseAssets, releaseUrl } from "../lib/release";
import { SPELLED } from "../lib/lessons";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const release = latestRelease();
const assets = releaseAssets(release);
const history = releases();

/* The command a reader runs by hand is the command the installer runs, with
 * the tool it prefers first. Assembled from what scripts/download.mjs read out
 * of install.sh, never typed. */
const [preferred] = download.checkers;
const digestCommand = (file: string) =>
  [preferred.tool, preferred.args, file].filter(Boolean).join(" ");

/* The machine each asset is for, as install.sh's own case arms name it: the
 * `uname` pair it accepts and the target it turns that into. */
const machineOf = (target: string) =>
  download.accepted.find((entry) => entry.target === target) ?? null;
---

<Page
  kind="TechArticle"
  title="Download"
  summary="Every iyi release, the tarball for each machine, and how the installer verifies one before it unpacks anything: it downloads the release's checksum file, refuses a tarball that does not match, and leaves nothing behind when it refuses."
>
  <section class="wrap head">
    <p class="label">Download, <a href={releaseUrl(release)}>version {release.version}</a></p>
    <h1>A tarball per machine, and a checksum the installer will not skip.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A release publishes one relocatable tarball per machine and one{" "}
      <code>{download.checksums}</code> file beside them. The installer
      downloads that file, compares it, and unpacks nothing when it does not
      match. Installing by hand, the same check is one command and one look.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a class="cta" href={releaseUrl(release)}>Release {release.version}, {release.date}</a>
      <a class="cta ghost" href={`${base}install/`}>The one-line installer</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>The artifacts</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Named the way the installer names them, from the version the changelog
      states. Each row is what you download, the machine it is for, and the
      command that prints its digest.
    </p>
    <ul class="assets">
      {assets.map((asset) => {
        const machine = machineOf(asset.target);
        return (
          <li>
            <div class="asset-head">
              <span class="machine">{asset.machine}</span>
              <span class="uname">
                {machine ? `uname says ${machine.uname}` : "no case arm in the installer"}
              </span>
            </div>
            <a class="url" href={asset.url}><code>{asset.file}</code></a>
            <p class="verify">
              <span class="label">verify</span>
              <code>{digestCommand(asset.file)}</code>
            </p>
          </li>
        );
      })}
    </ul>
    <p class="sub">
      What that prints has to equal the line for the same file in{" "}
      <a href={releaseUrl(release)}><code>{download.checksums}</code></a>, which
      is attached to the release. This site does not restate the digests: it
      cannot read them at build time, and a hash copied by hand is exactly the
      thing a hash exists to catch. They are on the release page, beside the
      files they are about.
    </p>
    <p class="sub">
      Where <code>{preferred.tool}</code> is missing, the installer falls back
      to{" "}
      {download.checkers.slice(1).map((checker) => (
        <code>{[checker.tool, checker.args].filter(Boolean).join(" ")}</code>
      ))}
      , and refuses to continue when neither is there.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What the installer checks, in its own words</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      This is the passage, not a summary of it. Note the last branch: a release
      that published no checksum file is said out loud rather than passed over.
    </p>
    <Lifted
      text={download.passages.verify.text}
      caption="install.sh, download and verify"
      cite={download.passages.verify.cite}
    />
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h3>The file it looks for is the file CI writes</h3>
        <p class="sub">
          The release job computes the digests over the tarballs it is about to
          attach, and attaches them too. The installer's name for that file and
          the job's name for it are checked against each other when this page
          is generated: if they ever differ, the site fails to build rather
          than telling you a tarball was verified.
        </p>
        <Lifted
          text={download.passages.publish.text}
          caption="the release job"
          cite={download.passages.publish.cite}
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>And the refusal is tested</h3>
        <p class="sub">
          Before any of that ships, CI corrupts one digit of the published
          checksum file, runs the installer against it, and requires three
          things: that it fails, that it fails with its own sentence, and that
          no binary is left behind.
        </p>
        <Lifted
          text={download.passages.tamper.text}
          caption="the gate over the installer"
          cite={download.passages.tamper.cite}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Machines it refuses</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Releases ship {download.accepted.map((entry) => entry.target).join(" and ")},
      and the installer names what it will not do rather than guessing. Anything
      else gets this sentence and a pointer to building from source:
    </p>
    <p class="refusal"><code>{download.refused}</code></p>
    <Lifted
      text={download.passages.refusal.text}
      caption="install.sh, the uname case"
      cite={download.passages.refusal.cite}
    />
    <p class="sub">
      Other platforms build from source. The compiler cross-compiles for{" "}
      <a href={`${base}targets/`}><Measure of="targets" /> targets</a>; these
      are the ones a release job produces a tarball for.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>The knobs</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      The script documents {SPELLED[download.knobs.length]} environment
      variables and reads exactly those:
    </p>
    <dl class="knobs">
      {download.knobs.map((knob) => (
        <div class="knob">
          <dt><code>{knob.name}</code></dt>
          <dd>
            <p>{knob.explanation}</p>
            {knob.fallback ? (
              <p class="default">defaults to <code>{knob.fallback}</code></p>
            ) : (
              <p class="default">unset by default</p>
            )}
          </dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <Lifted
      text={download.passages.knobs.text}
      caption="install.sh, the header"
      cite={download.passages.knobs.cite}
    />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Every release</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      The notes for each are on its own page in the repository, written from
      the tag's own message. This site does not publish the changelog.
    </p>
    <ul class="history">
      {history.map((entry) => (
        <li>
          <a href={releaseUrl(entry)}><code>{entry.version}</code></a>
          <span>{entry.date}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap next">
    <h2>Then</h2>
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a class="cta" href={`${base}install/`}>Install it</a>
      <a class="cta ghost" href={`${base}agents/`}>For your agents</a>
      <a class="cta ghost" href={`${base}playground/`}>Try it first</a>
    </div>
    <dl class="evidence">
      <dt>generated by</dt>
      <dd>{download.provenance.generator}</dd>
      <dt>quoted from</dt>
      <dd>{download.provenance.source}</dd>
      <dt>at commit</dt>
      <dd>{download.provenance.commit}</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <style>
    section {
      padding-block: clamp(1.2rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    }

    .head {
      padding-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    }

    .head h1 {
      font-size: var(--step-4);
      margin-block: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
      max-width: 22ch;
    }

    .lede {
      color: var(--graphite);
      max-width: 62ch;
      margin-block-end: 1.4rem;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: var(--step-2);
      margin-block-end: 0.6rem;
    }

    h3 {
      font-size: var(--step-0);
      margin-block-end: 0.4rem;
    }

    .sub {
      color: var(--graphite);
      max-width: 62ch;
      margin-block-end: 1rem;
    }

    /* One block per tarball: machine, file, and the command that checks it.
     * The command is on the page rather than in a paragraph about it, because
     * a reader who is verifying is at a prompt. */
    .assets {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 24rem), 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .assets li {
      border: var(--hair) solid var(--hairline);
      border-radius: 2px;
      padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
      background: var(--raise);
    }

    .asset-head {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.2rem 1rem;
    }

    .machine {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .uname {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: var(--step--2);
      color: var(--mute);
    }

    .assets .url {
      display: block;
      margin-block: 0.45rem;
      word-break: break-all;
    }

    .verify {
      margin: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .refusal {
      max-width: 70ch;
      margin-block-end: 1rem;
    }

    .refusal code {
      white-space: normal;
    }

    .cols {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
      gap: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
      align-items: start;
    }

    .knobs {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.8rem;
      max-width: 62ch;
    }

    .knob {
      padding-block-end: 0.7rem;
      border-block-end: var(--hair) solid var(--hairline);
    }

    .knob dd {
      margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
      color: var(--graphite);
    }

    .knob p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    .default {
      font-size: var(--step--1);
      color: var(--mute);
      margin-block-start: 0.2rem;
    }

    .history {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 14rem), 1fr));
      gap: 0.35rem 1.5rem;
      max-width: 60rem;
    }

    .history li {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.8rem;
      padding-block-end: 0.35rem;
      border-block-end: var(--hair) solid var(--hairline);
      color: var(--graphite);
      font-size: var(--step--1);
    }

    .next {
      padding-block-end: 3rem;
    }

    .hero-cta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.8rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-block-end: 1.5rem;
    }
  </style>
</Page>
